@startuml
!include ../shortfall/style.iuml
title Execution: confirm with the user, then delete
autonumber

actor "User" as User
participant "MishMash" as App
participant "delete: DeleteRecipeCommand" as Delete
participant "book: RecipeBook" as Book

note over App, Delete : Parsing has produced a delete command for index 2; dispatch and index validation are condensed.
App -> Delete : confirmationPrompt(book)
activate Delete
Delete -> Book : size()
Book --> Delete : recipeCount
alt book is empty, or index exceeds recipeCount
  Delete --> App : throws MishMashException
  note over App, Delete : No question is asked and nothing is deleted. The caller displays the error.
else the recipe at index exists
  Delete -> Book : getRecipes()
  Book --> Delete : recipes (read-only copy)
  Delete --> App : Optional of "Are you sure you want to delete recipe 2: name? (y/n)"
  deactivate Delete
  App -> User : display the question
  User --> App : next input line
  alt answer is "y" or "yes", in any letter case
    App -> Delete : execute(book)
    activate Delete
    note over Delete, Book : findTarget repeats the size and index checks, because execute can also be called without a prompt.
    Delete -> Book : remove(index - 1)
    Book --> Delete : deleted recipe
    Delete --> App : "Recipe deleted!", the name, and "Recipes remaining: n"
    deactivate Delete
    App -> User : display the result
  else any other answer, or no more input
    App -> User : display "Cancelled. Nothing was changed."
    note over App, Book : execute is never called, so the book is unchanged.
  end
end

note over Delete, Book
  Logging and getter details are condensed. ActiveMealPlan is not involved, so an existing
  plan and its grocery list keep their original recipes.
end note
@enduml
